(in-ns 'go.arbace.hs) ^{:go/comments [[13 1 "// Cmm on hsi (doc/haskell/HASKELL-EVAL-SURVEY.md, \"HES67's design: Cmm on hsi\"): a program's own Cmm, the forms of"] [14 1 "// arbace.repr.haskell.cmm (one (cmm FILE TOP...) a file), loaded by hsi run --cmm FILE and interpreted over the machine's"] [15 1 "// memory. The model is x86_64's GHC's as far as the forms reach: GHC's global registers (R1-R10, F1-F6 and D1-D6 on XMM1-XMM6,"] [16 1 "// L1, Sp, Hp, BaseReg and the rest) as words, NativeNodeCall's and NativeReturn's assignment of arguments and results to them"] [17 1 "// (GHC.Cmm.CallConv), a stack in crt's memory whose top word is the return address of the Haskell code that called, every value"] [18 1 "// a word (a float its IEEE bits), the MachOps at their widths. A heap object a Cmm function is given (a gcptr argument) is a"] [19 1 "// word of the object window: objBase + its index << 32, the object's bytes at offsets from it as GHC lays them out where hsi"] [20 1 "// knows the layout (a byte array: its header word, its size, its payload at SIZEOF_StgArrBytes); a code label is a word of the"] [21 1 "// code window. A foreign \"C\" call calls the program's own C (ci) or hsi's table of C functions; a primcall of the Haskell"] [22 1 "// (foreign import prim) whose label hsi's own primcalls lack runs the Cmm procedure of that name."] [25 43 "// code labels: cmmCodeBase + 16 * index (nothing is mapped there)"] [26 43 "// heap objects: cmmObjBase + index << 32"] [30 1 "// the global registers (GHC.Cmm.Reg's GlobalReg) by index"] [32 16 "// R1 is gR0 + 1 ... R10"] [33 16 "// XMM1 (F1, D1) is gX0 + 1 ... XMM6"] [53 1 "// cmmTy is a CmmType: its width in bits, float or not, a GC pointer or not."] [95 1 "// cmmExpr is a compiled expression: its value, a word, and its type."] [118 1 "// cmmStmt is a compiled statement."] [121 13 "// an assignment's local, or its global register"] [124 13 "// goto's and a branch's targets (statement indexes)"] [136 1 "// cmmProc is a procedure: its formals (their locals and types), its locals' count, its statements."] [143 19 "// the 'return' convention (NativeReturn)"] [148 1 "// cmmProg is the machine's Cmm: its procedures, its data, its registers, its stack and its windows' tables."] [162 1 "// cmmProgs are the machines' Cmm (one machine a process; a table, so that machine.go's Machine is unchanged)."] [167 1 "// cmmFiles and cmmMain are the driver's --cmm FILE and --cmm-main (CmmArgs)."] [173 1 "// CmmArgs takes the driver's Cmm options out of hsi run's arguments: --cmm FILE (a file of Cmm forms, loaded before main"] [174 1 "// runs) and --cmm-main (the program's main is Cmm's ZCMain_main_closure)."] [193 1 "// RunMain runs the program: its Cmm loaded first, then its Haskell main, or its Cmm main."] [208 1 "// cmmAct is a procedure's activation: its locals."] [216 1 "// LoadCmm loads a file of Cmm forms (arbace.repr.haskell.cmm's output): its data laid out in crt's memory, its procedures"] [217 1 "// compiled. The labels resolve once every file is loaded (the first call)."] [250 4 "// first every label (the data's addresses, the procedures' code addresses), then the procedures' code"] [277 1 "// cmmData lays out a section's datum: its statics in order (a string NUL-terminated, as .string emits it)."] [314 1 "// cmmClosure is a static closure (Parser.y's CLOSURE): its info pointer, then its payload."] [326 1 "// cmmLit is a static literal's word."] [350 1 "// cmmLabel is a label's word: the program's data or code, else a C symbol (the RTS's, C's: hsi's label table)."] [371 1 "// cmmProcCompile compiles a procedure's form."] [585 1 "// fbits is a float's bits at width w."] [607 1 "// cmmMachOp is a MachOp (GHC.Cmm.MachOp) at its widths: ws its width, or a conversion's from and to."] [631 3 "// exact: non-zero when the signed product does not fit the width (Note [MO_S_MulMayOflo significant width])"] [639 34 "// |result| at most 2^(w-1) when negative, 2^(w-1)-1 when not"] [714 3 "// amd64's minsd and maxsd: the first operand when it is less (greater), else the second"] [778 3 "// amd64's cvttsd2si (cvttss2si) at 32 or 64 bits, a narrower result its low bits: out of range and NaN give the"] [779 3 "// indefinite integer"] [805 1 "// ---- memory: crt's, and the object window"] [807 1 "// cmmObj is a heap object's word (the object window), made once."] [818 1 "// objAt is the object a word of the object window points into, and the offset."] [827 1 "// objBytes is the bytes of the object at offset off, n of them, as GHC lays a byte array out: its info word (none here:"] [828 1 "// zero), its size in bytes, its payload from SIZEOF_StgArrBytes (16)."] [885 1 "// ---- the calls"] [887 1 "// cmmArgRegs assigns values to registers as GHC.Cmm.CallConv's assignArgumentsPos does on x86_64 (NativeNodeCall,"] [888 1 "// NativeReturn: the vanilla registers R1-R6 for words and pointers, XMM1-XMM6 for floats and doubles, one count each):"] [889 1 "// the registers' indexes; a value past them is a stack argument, which hsi's Cmm does not lay out."] [911 1 "// cmmPrimcall is the code of a primcall the Haskell makes of the Cmm procedure lbl (foreign import prim): its non-void"] [912 1 "// arguments in registers, the procedure run until it returns to the Haskell (its stack's return address), its results"] [913 1 "// read from the registers by reps."] [929 1 "// cmmPrimopReps are the Cmm primcalls' results' representations, by their codes; cmmPrimMu guards it and cmmPrimcalls."] [935 1 "// cmmImageName is a primop's name in an image (image.go): a Cmm primcall's its label and results, which cmmImagePrimcall"] [936 1 "// reads back."] [947 1 "// cmmImagePrimcall is the primcall an image names: hsi's own, or a Cmm primcall (cmmImageName's)."] [960 1 "// cmmReps is a primcall form's REPS (STG-SPEC §3: one representation as itself, none as :v, several a vector)."] [984 1 "// cmmPrimcalls are the primcalls' codes made (compile.go and the images: one per label and results)"] [988 2 "// (the modules compile in parallel: hsi image's jobs)"] [1001 1 "// CmmCall calls the Cmm procedure lbl with the Haskell's values as (void ones dropped), its results as reps give them."] [1037 2 "// the results (NativeReturn)"] [1087 1 "// cmmRun runs p and what it jumps to until a jump to the return address."] [1101 1 "// cmmTarget is the procedure a jump to the word a goes to, nil for the return address."] [1113 1 "// cmmExec runs an activation's statements: the procedure it jumps to, nil when it returns to the Haskell."] [1154 4 "// mkReturn: the results in registers (NativeReturn), then a jump to the return address at the stack's top"] [1186 1 "// cmmCCall is a foreign \"C\" call: the program's own C (ci), else hsi's table of C functions and the RTS's below, else a"] [1187 1 "// function pointer's."] [1254 1 "// cmmRTS are the RTS's C functions a Cmm file calls that hsi's table does not have (rts/RtsStartup.c, rts/RtsMessages.c)."] [1256 2 "// stg_exit: C's exit, the C stdio flushed (not the Haskell handles: hs_exit is not called)"] [1262 2 "// _assertFail: barf's message (rtsFatalInternalErrorFn), then abort()"] [1273 1 "// cmmPrim is a callish MachOp (prim %NAME)."] [1332 1 "// cmmMove copies n bytes from src to dst, overlapping or not (memmove; memcpy too)."] [1343 1 "// cmmMacro is a statement macro (Parser.y's stmtMacros): the argument registers saved into and restored from BaseReg's"] [1344 1 "// register table (hsi's layout: R1-R10 at words 0-9, XMM1-XMM6 at words 10-15)."] [1372 1 "// RunCmm runs a program whose main is Cmm (all.T's cmm_src: the .cmm defines ZCMain_main_closure): hs_main's"] [1373 1 "// rts_evalLazyIO entering the closure, its info pointer's code run with R1 the closure; its end the program's (a return"] [1374 1 "// flushes the handles, as hs_exit)."]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[177 12] [177 27] [196 25] [237 21] [238 29] [353 23] [356 24] [377 39] [383 40] [394 20] [416 24] [456 25] [471 29] [493 29] [809 24] [849 36] 