;; Cmm on hsi (doc/haskell/HASKELL-EVAL-SURVEY.md, "HES67's design: Cmm on hsi"): a program's own Cmm, the forms of
;; arbace.repr.haskell.cmm (one (cmm FILE TOP...) a file), loaded by hsi run --cmm FILE and interpreted over the machine's
;; memory. The model is x86_64's GHC's as far as the forms reach: GHC's global registers (R1-R10, F1-F6 and D1-D6 on XMM1-XMM6,
;; L1, Sp, Hp, BaseReg and the rest) as words, NativeNodeCall's and NativeReturn's assignment of arguments and results to them
;; (GHC.Cmm.CallConv), a stack in crt's memory whose top word is the return address of the Haskell code that called, every value
;; a word (a float its IEEE bits), the MachOps at their widths. A heap object a Cmm function is given (a gcptr argument) is a
;; word of the object window: objBase + its index << 32, the object's bytes at offsets from it as GHC lays them out where hsi
;; knows the layout (a byte array: its header word, its size, its payload at SIZEOF_StgArrBytes); a code label is a word of the
;; code window. A foreign "C" call calls the program's own C (ci) or hsi's table of C functions; a primcall of the Haskell
;; (foreign import prim) whose label hsi's own primcalls lack runs the Cmm procedure of that name.

^{:go/pos {:lparen [24 7] :rparen [28 1] :tok-pos [24 1]}} (go/const
  [^{:val 3458764513820540928 :go/pos {:name-pos [25 2]}} cmmCodeBase ^{:go/apos {2 [25 23]} :go/atext {2 "0x3000000000000000"} :go/pos {:lparen [25 22] :rparen [25 41]}} (conv ^{:go/pos {:name-pos [25 16]}} uint64 0x3000000000000000)] ; code labels: cmmCodeBase + 16 * index (nothing is mapped there)
  [^{:val 4611686018427387904 :go/pos {:name-pos [26 2]}} cmmObjBase ^{:go/apos {2 [26 23]} :go/atext {2 "0x4000000000000000"} :go/pos {:lparen [26 22] :rparen [26 41]}} (conv ^{:go/pos {:name-pos [26 16]}} uint64 0x4000000000000000)] ; heap objects: cmmObjBase + index << 32
  [^{:val 65536 :go/pos {:name-pos [27 2]}} cmmStackSz ^{:go/apos {1 [27 16] 2 [27 21]} :go/pos {:op-pos [27 18]}} (<< 1 16)])



